// globals.marco — global commands ported from MacroMarco's globals module,
// driven by hotkey events. Run as a persistent server and pipe Hotkeys events
// (from a host that captures the backtick leader key, e.g. bridges/ahk-hotkeys.ahk)
// to its stdin:
//
//   bridges\ahk-hotkeys.ahk | marco serve --host windows programs/globals.marco
//
// Faithful to globals.ahk: `e` spams E until stop, `c` spams click until stop,
// Esc/stop ends the spam; 1-4 press hotbar keys 5-8. The spam runs in the host
// (one loop at a time, exactly like the original engine) so it persists across
// events until Stop.

use os.

// Inbound global-hotkey events (host -> Marco). A host capturing the backtick
// leader key writes lines like {"feed":"Hotkeys","event":"E"}.
the Hotkeys is a feed of any.

// A spam request: fill Key (to spam a key) or Button (to spam a click).
the SpamCmd is a set.
this's Key is a text.
this's Button is a text.
this's Every is a number.

the Globals is an actor.

// `e` — spam the E key until stop (CONFIG.defaultKeySpamMs = 50).
this can SpamE.
this's SpamE does...
    the cmd is a SpamCmd with Key "e", Every 50.
    do OS's Spam with cmd.
    this is ok!

// `c` — spam left click until stop (CONFIG.defaultClickSpamMs = 50).
this can SpamClick.
this's SpamClick does...
    the cmd is a SpamCmd with Button "left", Every 50.
    do OS's Spam with cmd.
    this is ok!

// Esc / stop — end the running spam.
this can StopAll.
this's StopAll does...
    do OS's StopSpam.
    this is ok!

// Hotbar: 1-4 press keys 5-8 once (globals.ahk Send5..Send8).
this can Hotbar1.
this's Hotbar1 does...
    do OS's Key with "5".
    this is ok!
this can Hotbar2.
this's Hotbar2 does...
    do OS's Key with "6".
    this is ok!
this can Hotbar3.
this's Hotbar3 does...
    do OS's Key with "7".
    this is ok!
this can Hotbar4.
this's Hotbar4 does...
    do OS's Key with "8".
    this is ok!

// Leader-key command routing.
when Hotkeys reads E?
    do Globals's SpamE...
        when ok?
            log "spamming e".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads C?
    do Globals's SpamClick...
        when ok?
            log "spamming click".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads Stop?
    do Globals's StopAll...
        when ok?
            log "stopped".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads K1?
    do Globals's Hotbar1...
        when ok?
            log "sent 5".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads K2?
    do Globals's Hotbar2...
        when ok?
            log "sent 6".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads K3?
    do Globals's Hotbar3...
        when ok?
            log "sent 7".
        or?
            log that's error.

when Hotkeys reads K4?
    do Globals's Hotbar4...
        when ok?
            log "sent 8".
        or?
            log that's error.

the App is a script.
log "globals ready".
